Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:19:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] drm/bridge: inno-hdmi: Add HDMI audio support

The Innosilicon HDMI transmitter has an I2S audio input with its own
sample rate, I2S mode and audio clock regeneration (N/CTS) registers,
which are already defined in this driver but never used.

Implement the DRM bridge HDMI audio callbacks: program the sample rate,
the number of I2S lanes and N/CTS (from drm_hdmi_acr_get_n_cts() for the
current TMDS character rate) on prepare and again after every mode set,
mute and unmute through the AV mute register, and send the audio
infoframe through the AAI packet buffer. The drm_bridge_connector then
registers the generic HDMI codec.

Audio is only exposed when the platform data says the integration feeds
the I2S input, so existing users are unchanged.

